IO-54: report the smallest flow a pump delivered in the Pumping Summary

DefaultReportPlugin printed a literal 0.0 in the Min Flow column of the
Pumping Summary. Keep the smallest flow of the steps in which the pump ran
(flow above 0.001 cfs, the legacy MIN_RUNOFF_FLOW test) in a new
LinkData::stat_pump_min_flow and print it; a pump that never runs still
reports 0.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-54_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
index 839529d..4bd96d2 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
@@ -5443,6 +5443,10 @@ void SWMMEngine::updateStatistics(double dt_routing) noexcept {
             if (is_on) {
                 ctx_.links.stat_pump_on_time[uj] += dt_routing;
                 ctx_.links.stat_pump_volume[uj] += q * dt_routing;
+                // smallest running flow, over the steps legacy counts as on
+                // (q > MIN_RUNOFF_FLOW, stats.c)
+                double& qmin = ctx_.links.stat_pump_min_flow[uj];
+                if (q > 0.001 && (qmin == 0.0 || q < qmin)) qmin = q;
 
                 // Pump energy (kWh), matching legacy link_getPower:
                 //   power_kW = |dh| * |q| / 8.814 * KWperHP ; energy += power_kW * dt/3600
